---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How we work"
  description="Orb’s four-step AEO method: audit, on-site citability, off-site mentions, and prompt panel measurement."
  path="/how-we-work"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">How Orb works</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A practical loop: understand how answer engines talk about you today,
        harden on-site citability, earn corroborating mentions, then measure
        with a living prompt panel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="steps">
        <article class="step">
          <div class="card-num">01</div>
          <h3>Audit</h3>
          <p>
            Map category prompts, current answers, competitors cited, and gaps
            in your entity footprint. Establish a baseline for found / cited /
            correct—before changing anything.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div class="card-num">02</div>
          <h3>On-site citability</h3>
          <p>
            Rewrite and structure pages so claims are answer-first in HTML:
            clear definitions, FAQs that match real questions, schema that
            mirrors visible copy, technical crawl health.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div class="card-num">03</div>
          <h3>Off-site mentions</h3>
          <p>
            Build corroboration where answer engines and humans already look:
            references, listings, expert quotes, and partner pages that name
            you consistently—not spammy link schemes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="step">
          <div class="card-num">04</div>
          <h3>Prompt panel</h3>
          <p>
            Run a fixed set of prompts on a schedule. Score whether you are
            found, cited, and correctly described. Feed misses back into the
            audit. See Measurement for the methodology.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow prose">
      <h2>What you get in practice</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Baseline report: how engines currently describe your category</li>
        <li>Prioritized page and entity fixes for citability</li>
        <li>Off-site mention plan aligned to real corroboration gaps</li>
        <li>Prompt panel setup and a cadence for review</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we won’t do</h2>
      <p>
        We won’t promise rankings inside proprietary models, fabricate case
        studies, or optimize for deceptive answers. Orb’s Hong Kong experiment
        is deliberately measurement-honest: results are published when they
        exist—not invented to fill a landing page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-band glow-border">
        <h2>Start with an audit</h2>
        <p>
          Share your category and a few prompts customers already ask. We’ll
          tell you what’s found, cited, and correct today.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content: center;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@orb.example"
            >Talk to Orb</a
          >
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/measurement">Measurement details</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
